From: FongMi <b8892778@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 23:42:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] avformat/hls: normalize timestamps across discontinuities

Keep audio and video packet timestamps continuous when HLS ad splices reset or restore their native timeline. Re-anchor the correction after seeks and cover both discontinuity directions with focused tests.

(cherry picked from commit 5805f9364c2e9a5f6ce625c9077b308c3ed4014d)

Ported from FongMi/FFmpeg@5805f9364c2e9a5f6ce625c9077b308c3ed4014d

[IOS-POC-26-2b backport to n8.1.2: git 3-way merge applied it without conflicts;
 every added/removed line is identical to the original commit (only context
 differs: the hls_read_seek() context line "pls->input_reuse = 0;" comes from
 0616685b1e, which is not backported). hls_timestamp.{c,h} and
 tests/hls_timestamp.c are byte-identical to FongMi/FFmpeg@5805f9364c.]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
